# RunPod mutate

## Gate

Load only when the user authorized RunPod **and** used an explicit mutate
verb this turn (**create**, **start**, **stop**, **restart**, **delete**,
**update**, **cancel**, **deploy**, **run**) naming the object or clear
create fields. Otherwise stay on `runpod-inventory`. Always pair with
`runpod-safety` before any mutate tool.

Prefer namespace `user-mcp_runpod`. Never invent tool names or resource ids.

## Inventory before mutate

1. List matching pods/endpoints/templates/volumes **this turn**
   (`runpod-inventory`).
2. Resolve every id from MCP or user paste — never guess.
3. For create: `list-gpu-types` / `get-capacity` (and data centers when
   region matters) before `create-pod` / `create-endpoint`.
4. State planned action + cost impact in one line; then call the mutate tool.

## Live mutate tool map

| Action | Tool | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Create pod | `create-pod` | `gpuTypeIds` or `computeType`; `imageName` or `templateId`; cost while running |
| Update pod | `update-pod` | resolved pod id + fields user named |
| Start / stop / restart pod | `start-pod` / `stop-pod` / `restart-pod` | resolved pod id |
| Delete pod | `delete-pod` | permanent — explicit **delete** |
| Create endpoint | `create-endpoint` | image + `gpuPoolIds` from `list-gpu-types` `pool` |
| Update endpoint | `update-endpoint` | resolved endpoint id |
| Set endpoint GPUs | `set-endpoint-gpus` | pool ids from inventory |
| Delete endpoint | `delete-endpoint` | permanent |
| Purge endpoint queue | `purge-endpoint-queue` | explicit purge verb |
| Run / runsync endpoint | `run-endpoint` / `runsync-endpoint` | job invoke |
| Cancel / retry job | `cancel-job` / `retry-job` | resolved job id |
| Deploy hub repo | `deploy-hub-repo` | repo from `list-hub-repos` |
| Create / update / delete template | `create-template` / `update-template` / `delete-template` | |
| Create / update / delete volume | `create-network-volume` / `update-network-volume` / `delete-network-volume` | size 10–4096 GB; tier immutable after create |
| Registry auth create / delete | `create-container-registry-auth` / `delete-container-registry-auth` | never echo password/token in chat |
| Registry delegation create / delete | `create-registry-delegation` / `delete-registry-delegation` | ECR ARN path |

## Defaults

- Prefer the cheapest GPU type that meets the stated need; cite
  `list-gpu-types` / `get-capacity` evidence.
- Prefer stop or scale-to-zero when the user did not ask to leave GPU time
  running.
- Default image when neither image nor template given and user wants a
  general PyTorch pod: `runpod/pytorch:1.0.2-cu1281-torch280-ubuntu2404`
  (per MCP create-pod guidance) — state that default in the receipt.
- SSH: only pass `sshPublicKey` as the **public** key contents when the user
  provided it — never invent or paste private keys.
- State which defaults you relied on in the receipt.

## Delete / cost discipline

- Delete pod/endpoint/volume/template/auth: explicit **delete** + resolved id.
- Create/start: warn that GPU time bills while running.
- Registry auth: refuse to print password/token back; confirm id only.

## Operator receipt (mutate)

- action (create/start/stop/delete/update/run/…)
- resource id(s) + name
- GPU / image / pool summary
- cost note (running vs stopped)
- no API keys, registry passwords, or env secret values

